<title>FRANCE: Remy-Cointreau 1997/98 Q1 sales up 13 pct.</title>
<headline>Remy-Cointreau 1997/98 Q1 sales up 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Total					  1,448  vs	   1,277</p>
<p>    Cognac					   376  vs	     358</p>
<p>    Liqueurs and spirits			 257  vs	     226</p>
<p>    Wines and cask making			218  vs	     176</p>
<p>    Champagne					171  vs	     145</p>
<p>    Partner brands				 426  vs	     372</p>
<p>NOTE - Remy-Cointreau said in its 1996/97 earnings statement that first quarter turnover to the end of June rose 13.4 percent to 1.45 billion francs.</p>
<p>It said first-quarter turnover showed growth in all divisions. &quot;This performance reflects the good health of the brands and the dynamism of the commercial network,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
